    "image": "/images/kitestring-alternative.png",
    "content": "\nIf you're searching for a **Kitestring alternative**, you've already discovered the problem: Kitestring is gone.\n\nThe service quietly shut down at some point after its 2014 launch, leaving behind a lot of broken links and a lot of people who relied on it. If you found Kitestring through an old article — a \"best safety apps\" list, a blog post from a running community, a Reddit thread — that recommendation is out of date.\n\nThe good news: what Kitestring did is simple, and **CheckIn More's Safety Timers do the same thing** — with a real mobile app, modern reliability, and a free plan to get started.\n\n---\n\n## What Kitestring Did\n\nKitestring was straightforward. You'd set a timer before heading out alone — a run, a hike, a first date, a walk home at night. If you didn't check back in when the timer expired, Kitestring would text your emergency contacts.\n\nThat's it. No GPS. No location sharing. Just a countdown and an SMS safety net.\n\nIt was a genuinely good idea, built as a website and SMS service at a time when personal safety apps were rare. Thousands of people used it. And then it disappeared.\n\n---\n\n## CheckIn More Safety Timers: The Direct Replacement\n\nCheckIn More's **Safety Timers** were built for exactly this use case. The mechanics will feel immediately familiar if you ever used Kitestring:\n\n1. Set a duration — \"45 minutes,\" \"back by 10pm,\" \"2 hours\"\n2. Go do your thing\n3. Check back in when you're safe\n4. If you don't check in, your contacts are notified automatically\n\nThe key differences: CheckIn More is a native mobile app (not just a website), supports email, SMS, and phone call alerts, and is actively maintained.\n\n### Text to Start a Timer — Just Like Kitestring\n\nOne thing Kitestring users loved was the ability to manage everything over SMS, without logging into a website. CheckIn More supports this too:\n\n- **\"45m going for a run\"**\n- **\"date night, back by 10:30\"**\n- **\"heading to the trailhead, 2 hours\"**\n\nWhen you're home safe, just text back something like \"just got home\" or \"I'm back\" to cancel the timer. If plans change mid-trip, text \"need 30 more minutes\" or \"running late.\"\n\n### A Grace Period That Makes Sense\n\nWhen your timer expires, CheckIn More waits **5 minutes** before notifying your contacts. Life doesn't run on the minute — the timer ending doesn't mean something is wrong, it means you haven't checked in yet. The grace period keeps things from feeling like a false alarm every time you're slightly late.\n\n---\n\n## How Notifications Work\n\nWhen a timer expires without a check-in, your contacts are notified through whichever channels your plan includes:\n\n| Plan | Price | How Contacts Are Notified |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Free** | Free | Email to 1 contact |\n| **Plus** | $6.99/month | Email + SMS to unlimited contacts |\n| **Premium** | $19.99/month | Email + SMS + AI phone call to unlimited contacts |\n\nKitestring only sent SMS alerts. CheckIn More gives you options — and the phone call tier is worth noting. If you're out late and your contact is asleep, a phone call is a lot harder to miss than a notification.\n\n---\n\n## What CheckIn More Adds Beyond Kitestring\n\nKitestring was built around a single use case: safety timers. CheckIn More does that, but it's also a full daily wellness check-in app. If you want a routine daily safety net on top of on-demand timers, it's all in one place.\n\n| Feature | Kitestring | CheckIn More |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Safety timers** | ✓ (web/SMS only) | ✓ (app + SMS on paid plans) |\n| **SMS alerts to contacts** | ✓ | ✓ (Plus and Premium) |\n| **Email alerts to contacts** | ✗ | ✓ (all plans) |\n| **Phone call alerts** | ✗ | ✓ (Premium) |\n| **Daily check-in schedule** | ✗ | ✓ |\n| **Mood status check-in** | ✗ | ✓ |\n| **Native mobile app** | ✗ (web only) | ✓ |\n| **Currently operational** | ✗ Shut down | ✓ Active |\n\n---\n\n## Who Is CheckIn More Best For?\n\nIf you're coming from Kitestring, Safety Timers in CheckIn More are the closest direct replacement. The free plan includes one safety timer per day — which for most situations is exactly what you need.\n\nIf you want unlimited timers, SMS alerts to multiple contacts, or the ability to manage timers via text message, the Plus plan at $6.99/month covers all of that.\n\n---\n\n## Ready to Replace Kitestring?\n\nThe free plan requires no credit card. Paid plans include a free trial.\n\n<DownloadButtons slug=\"kitestring-alternative\" />\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n**Why did Kitestring shut down?**\nKitestring launched in 2014 as a web and SMS-based safety service. It was never formally acquired or merged — it simply stopped operating around February 2024. No official shutdown announcement was made. The domain is no longer active as a safety service.\n\n**Does CheckIn More work the same way as Kitestring?**\nThe core mechanic is identical: set a timer, check back in when you're safe, and your contacts are notified if you don't. CheckIn More adds a native mobile app, email notifications, optional phone call alerts, and a full daily check-in system.\n\n**Do my contacts need to download anything?**\nNo. Your contacts receive alerts by email, SMS, or phone call. No app, no account required on their end.\n\n**Can I manage timers over text message?**\nYes, on Plus and Premium plans. You can start, extend, and cancel timers entirely via SMS — no need to open the app.\n\n**Is there a free plan?**\nYes. The free plan includes one safety timer per day and email alerts to one contact. No credit card required.\n\n---\n\n*Information current as of April 2026.*\n",
